-- title:
--   Tube-free rational places centre at non-supersingular j-values (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (the hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Further, $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ that are rational (the structural map from the base field to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The field data: `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, where `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with group `levelH q M'`; $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with residue target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` together with a surjective residue map onto that field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and satisfying the order-transport clauses recorded in that structure); and `hR₀` says that this reduction is the coefficientwise one: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (residue A) y`.
--
--   The Igusa family: $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$. Four hypotheses constrain it: `hIg_inf` characterises `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y = x$ after pushing forward along `A.subtype`; `hIg` says each line $\ell$ is `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says `OIg` is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`.
--
--   The supersingular family: `OSS` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each $s \in W$. Here `hSS_A` says that a constant of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `OSS s` exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $j$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in `OSS s` and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix` says each `OSS s` is invariant under pullback by `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in$ `OSS s` such that $t - a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The prolongation data: $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue target `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')`, subject to `hR` : `R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` : an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)`.
--
--   The arithmetic frame over the base: $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$. Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field, while `hκ` says that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Auxiliary level data: $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ is a valuation subring of $K_1$ whose elements are precisely those elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring and Henselian local.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for every $k_0$-subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ generate `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the field generated over $k_0$ by the image of $K'$ and $F_0$, the vanishing of $\sum_i c_i a_i$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$. Write $L_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$ together with $F_0$. An $A_1$-algebra structure on $L_1$ is assumed, compatible with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the sense that the image of $a \in A_1$ in `fieldBar q M'` is the constant attached to $a$ viewed in $K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Finally $j_1 \in L_1$ is an element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular $j$-function, transported by `hle`, and $j_1 \ne 0$.
--
--   Four auxiliary predicates are introduced for the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ L₁ j₁`, the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (elements of $L_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along their common middle. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in L_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart whose image under `ιFin`, respectively `ιInf`, is $x$, there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that for every $f \in L_1$ with `InStalk x f` one has $f \in$ `P.toValuationSubring`, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. A fourth predicate `GoodPt x` is also bound — $x$ maps to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ under `toBase`, $x$ is closed for specialisation, every element of either chart algebra whose image is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in each point of that chart above $x$, and for every $y$ in the finite chart above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ one has $\varphi(j_1) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω` — but it does not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   The assertion is then: for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is rational, and which lies in no supersingular tube in the sense that for no $s \in W$ is it the case that for all $f \in$ `R₀.integers` satisfying the $j$-regularity condition (non-negative order wherever `jq` has non-negative order) and having $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and all $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with `Centred P x`, every point $y$ of the finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A₁ L₁ j₁` with `ιFin`-image $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ L₁ j₁` to $\Omega$ whose kernel is the prime $y$, one has
--   $$\varphi\bigl(\mathrm{jChartFin}\ A_1\ L_1\ j_1\bigr) \notin \mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \Omega,$$
--   that is, the geometric $j$-value of $\mathfrak X_1$ at $y$ is not supersingular in the sense of `ssJSet`.
--
--   This is the converse direction of the supersingular-tube analysis on the two-chart integral model of the $j$-line in the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve, in the case $q = 2$: a rational place that specialises into none of the supersingular tubes indexed by $W$ can only be centred at points of the model lying over non-supersingular $j$-values. It is obtained from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssTube_of_residue_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssTube_of_residue_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_of_eq_two), which produces such a tube when the reduction of $j$ at $P$ is supersingular, together with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.inStalk_and_inMax_iff_mem_asIdeal_chartAlg_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.inStalk_and_inMax_iff_mem_asIdeal_chartAlg_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two), which identifies the value $\varphi(j_1)$ with that reduction; it is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_two).
